{{DISPLAYTITLE: <span class="text-evolution";">Evolved Witch</span>}}
{{Evolved Card Infobox|Cost=5|CycleCost=1|Cycles=1|Rarity=Epic|Type=Troop|Arena=P.E.K.K.A.'s Playhouse|ReleaseDate=5 May 2025}}
{{Quote|Your Skeletons are willing to sacrifice themselves for their beloved Witch, lending their souls and healing her when they're destroyed.}}

The Witch's Evolution is an {{Rarity|Epic}} [[Cards|card]] unlocked with 6 Evolution Shards. It spawns a Witch with identical stats to the original. Once a Skeleton that the Evolved Witch has spawned is defeated, she is healed. This healing can overheal, allowing her to achieve 24% more hitpoints at its maximum capacity. The Evolved Witch takes an appearance as a woman who has glowing pink eyes and violet eyebrows, wears a violet cloak with gold linings, a ram face on top and two horns on the sides and dress, a dark gray top, team-colored armlets, darker purple lipstick, and a belt with the [[Card Evolution]] symbol in the middle, and wields a staff with a skull on top. The Witch's Evolution costs 5 [[Elixir]] and requires 1 cycle to deploy.

==Strategy==
*Due to the Witch costing only 5 [[Elixir]] and requiring only 1 cycle to evolve, the player can evolve her multiple times in a match.
*The Evolved Witch naturally spawns [[Skeletons]] every 7 seconds. Due to her slower movement speed than the spawned Skeletons, the Evolved Witch would heal herself once her spawns cross the bridge when played behind the [[King's Tower]], allowing her to gain an advantage before engaging in fights against enemy units.
*A total of 3 Skeletons need to be defeated in order to have the Evolved Witch to from base health full overheal hitpoints, which can happen with just her first wave. This increases to total of 14 Skeleton that need to be defeated in order to have the Evolved Witch from 1 hitpoint to full overheal hitpoints, requiring a total of 4 waves, assuming no healing is wasted.
*Lighter [[:Category:Spell Cards|spells]] are less effective, as they'll usually defeat the Skeletons spawned around her, which can heal the Evolved Witch enough so that she has a decent amount of hitpoints. [[Poison]] in particular would take out two waves of Skeletons, which heal her even more. Trying to use [[Zap]] on her spawned Skeletons in order for a troop to break through her is also not very effective, as her health will be healed by their defeat. On the contrary, [[Rocket]] and [[Lightning]] are a far more effective way of taking her out, even though they are a -1 Elixir trade, as they will defeat her even if she is already at her maximum hitpoints.
*Playing her behind slow-moving units, like a [[Giant]], [[P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Golem]], or an [[Elixir Golem]] will allow her to support those cards with the spawned Skeletons, while also healing herself from their death, as they also move faster than the slow-moving troop of choice.
*Although splash units are great at wiping out her spawned Skeletons as well as other troops around her, they will have a harder time in defeating the Evolved Witch herself, since she would heal back with every Skeleton death, while she chips the opposing unit's health down. The [[Valkyrie]] is slightly more effective, as her hitpoints are elevated enough to survive the Evolved Witch's attacks.
*The Evolved Witch can also be played on decks with [[Balloon]] and [[Lava Hound]]. Her possible value will either bait Rocket or Lightning for the Balloon or support the Lava Hound + Balloon push with herself and her Skeletons.

